I'll try!

> panic
Something went horribly, horribly wrong with the program. You should
never see this.

> trickery
Something went slightly less horribly wrong. Often this is caused by
level files going missing unexpectedly; trickeries may be caused by the
OS or other programs, not necessarily NetHack.

> committed suicide
You tried to levelport to Level 0 (Nowhere). It's kind of amusing.

> crunched in the head by an iron ball
An iron ball fell on your head; I don't play with giant balls, so not
sure of the exact circumstances.

> died of exhaustion
"You die from hunger and exhaustion." - starved to death.

> dragged downstairs by an iron ball
Iron balls again; while it's still attached to your leg, it can fall
downstairs and drag you with it.

> killed [him/herself] with [his/her] bullwhip
Whipped yourself. Sicko.

> killed by an imperious order
Throne genocide.

> killed by an iron ball collision
What a load of balls; "The iron ball smacks into you!"

> killed by an unrefigerated sip of juice
Poisonous fountain, when you had Poison Resistance.

> killed by an unsuccessful polymorph
"Your new form doesn't seem healthy enough to survive..."
A polymorph set your HP or MaxHP to zero or less; if you'd had
Polymorph Control, you could've recovered slightly.

> killed by axing a hard object
Use a pick to break apart stone objects, axes are for trees. Trying to
use an axe on a stone object yields "The axe-handle vibrates
violently!" and you lose HP.

> killed by bumping into a wall (door, tree, boulder...)
> killed by crashing into iron bars
It's possible to go flying through the air in some situations, and lose
HP if you smack into something. "killed by touching the edge of the
universe" is another of these (hit a no-dig non-wall position).

> killed by dangerous winds
Something to do with ceasing to levitate in Sokoban. Need more
clarification.

> killed by elementary chemistry
Don't dip water into acid. NetHack acid is extremely strong, and you
know what happens if you attempt to dilute strong acids with water!

> killed by exhaustion
> killed by overexertion
Sleeping with an incubus or succubus can be bad for your health.

> petrified by elementary physics
You threw a cockatrice egg (AKA "stoning grenade") upwards. What goes
up, must come down.



